Registration and Leisure Management Department
System Overview
This system is designed to manage the complex logistical and educational operations of a community center. Unlike basic models, this system supports multi-resource allocation, allowing for flexible assignments where classes can involve multiple instructors, various locations, and interdisciplinary course affiliations.

Core Functionality
Advanced Course Mapping: Managing courses that can span multiple categories and group structures.

Dynamic Resource Scheduling: Handling complex Many-to-Many relationships between instructors, rooms, and class groups to maximize facility utility.

Enrollment & Capacity Tracking: Managing participant registration while monitoring real-time occupancy across different venues.

Data Model (ERD Entities)
The database is designed to support Many-to-Many (N:M) relationships through the following entities:

1. Base Entities
Courses: CourseID (PK), CourseName, Description, Price.

Instructors: InstructorID (PK), FullName, Phone, Specialization.

Rooms: RoomNumber (PK), MaxCapacity, Type.

Participants: ParticipantID (PK), FullName, DateOfBirth, Phone.

Groups: GroupID (PK), GroupName, DayOfWeek, StartTime.

2. Junction Entities (N:M Relationships)
To support your requirement for multiple assignments, we use the following junction tables:

Group_Instructors: Connects multiple instructors to a single group and vice versa.

Fields: GroupID (FK), InstructorID (FK).

Group_Rooms: Allows a group to be scheduled in different rooms (e.g., a lab for practice and a hall for lectures).

Fields: GroupID (FK), RoomNumber (FK).

Group_Courses: Links groups to one or more courses.

Fields: GroupID (FK), CourseID (FK).

Enrollment: Links participants to their chosen groups.

Fields: ParticipantID (FK), GroupID (FK), EnrollmentDate.


